      "status": "active",
      "color": "#8b5cf6",
      "created_at": "2026-03-14 18:09:50",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-21 03:30:45",
      "hourly_rate": 112.5,
      "narrative": "[{\"id\":\"legacy-0\",\"timestamp\":null,\"text\":\"3/20/2026 - 11am Teams meeting with the design team to discuss value engineering ideas to reduce costs. The general consensus at the council South Wing kickoff meeting was that the balcony is unnecessary. Without the balcony the building doesn't need to be as tall while we can vary the roof framing types to still effectively use the space above the new Lobby as originally proposed. The team agreed to take a few days after our meeting to digest and reconvene next week to continue the discussion. The general question we need input on from the council is the paradigm by which we should move forward. Specifically, we all know there is some concern regarding the amount of money we currently have available, and justifiably so; do we approach this as trying to build as much as we can within our current budget, if possible, or do we design for now and potential future needs knowing that more money will need to be raised? If you would like to provide input on this please reply to the entire council so everyone can see it.\"}]"
    }
  ],
